What HJViewer changes, since 2026-10-10:
- the patch series in server/patches and client/patches, each with its date and description;
- the replacement image files in client/overlay; the splash screen's line of text among them is
  glyph outlines of Noto Sans CJK KR (Copyright 2014-2021 Adobe, SIL Open Font License 1.1);
- the typeface of the app's text, Pretendard 1.3.9 (Regular, SemiBold and Bold, unmodified;
  https://github.com/orioncactus/pretendard), Copyright (c) 2021 Kil Hyung-jin, with Reserved
  Font Name Pretendard, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1: client/overlay puts the font files
  and their license into the app (flutter/assets/fonts), and each build's
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt repeats the license;
- at build time (.github/workflows/client-build.yml): the app version is set from
  client/version.env, the Android build switches to debug signing and more Gradle memory, the
  iOS build sets its own signing on the Runner target and drops entitlements the provisioning
  profile does not grant, and the Windows package ships the app as HJViewer.exe and leaves out
  RustDesk's printer driver and its closed-source adapter (remote printing is off).
Everything else in this repository is original work: hjv-api, the account service (server/api);
hjv-relay, the Wake-on-LAN relay (relay); and the scripts, tools, deploy files and docs. The client
workflow follows the steps of RustDesk's own CI.

